!! Real-world example: SaaS platform system context

This example shows a two-level C4 view of a SaaS analytics platform. The Context diagram (C4Context) shows external actors and system boundaries. The Container diagram (C4Container) zooms into the platform internals. Element types (Person, System, Container) are labeled inline — no additional legend is needed.

```
C4Context
    accTitle: SaaS analytics platform — system context
    accDescr: External users, the platform, and third-party dependencies

    %% ── External users ──────────────────────────
    Person(analyst, "Data Analyst", "Queries and visualises business data.")
    Person(admin, "Platform Admin", "Manages users, permissions, and billing.")
    Person_Ext(support, "Support Engineer", "Investigates incidents and data issues.")

    %% ── Core platform ───────────────────────────
    System(platform, "Analytics Platform", "Ingests, stores, and serves analytical queries over business events.")

    %% ── External dependencies ───────────────────
    System_Ext(auth0, "Auth0", "Handles user authentication and SSO.")
    System_Ext(stripe, "Stripe", "Processes subscription billing.")
    System_Ext(pagerduty, "PagerDuty", "Delivers on-call incident alerts.")
    System_Ext(s3, "AWS S3", "Long-term cold storage for raw event archives.")

    %% ── Relationships ───────────────────────────
    Rel(analyst,  platform,  "Runs queries and views dashboards", "HTTPS")
    Rel(admin,    platform,  "Manages users and billing", "HTTPS")
    Rel(support,  platform,  "Investigates data issues", "HTTPS")
    Rel(platform, auth0,     "Delegates authentication", "HTTPS / OIDC")
    Rel(platform, stripe,    "Manages subscriptions", "HTTPS / REST")
    Rel(platform, pagerduty, "Sends incident alerts", "HTTPS / REST")
    Rel(platform, s3,        "Archives raw events", "AWS SDK")
```

$$$text/vnd.tiddlywiki.mermaid
C4Context
